[{"id":"VRCE-6-34-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":1,"english":"As the monkeys and the Rākşasas thus faught on, the sun set, ant the fatal Night came.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"347eda9261d6ca4c68a80a8b551aca07452e7f4611d11ddfb85fcd3849bfff71","compact":"4ed47013cc521bc66383d4ecdd781a1818c705d55db3fe033f149265c855c489","nasal":"4ed47013cc521bc66383d4ecdd781a1818c705d55db3fe033f149265c855c489"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":2,"english":"Then commenced a night-engagement between the dreadful Rākşasas and the monkeys of fixed hostility, each party burning for victory.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.866,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9c190074ff25df46eec68d19dce8210bf6c7851a73f746c683e387985b68300b","compact":"4c7e0324e2d12e8f2861e1123c8f44b3430ba403432388db50ff1c64705d62fb","nasal":"4c7e0324e2d12e8f2861e1123c8f44b3430ba403432388db50ff1c64705d62fb"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":3,"english":"In that profound darkness, the monkeys and the Rākşasas began to slay each other, exclaiming, You are a Raksasa,' and 'you are a monkey.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.785,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1ad4c0e39c5136cb96bcdd4653a850b9a055b1c179bb17f8c56cb5f5430d29f3","compact":"b484b9201a6718d9066c8f02624bfde3606ea61b02841851acab78d6f582ae07","nasal":"b484b9201a6718d9066c8f02624bfde3606ea61b02841851acab78d6f582ae07"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":4,"english":"And in that army there was heard a mighty uproar of 'slain,' 'rive!\" 'come!' 'why fliest?'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.579,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e36661961b1cc52a0793680933b5670c8c03d2577d01a3991c4a7b028b30397d","compact":"574f40de466693122b49776a3f4bad25d487799b09a7333222ddf77b4b24aa77","nasal":"574f40de466693122b49776a3f4bad25d487799b09a7333222ddf77b4b24aa77"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":5,"english":"And, dark-hued, the Raksasas, equipped in golden mail, in that deep darkness appeared like elevated hills clad with woods of flaming incdicinal herbs.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.657,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21da34056961f4755ad7f525016b7fbb0eb2716eda873ad8a147d38ff1cbf590","compact":"667ccbeecc9085c44d8c0e0ccf8cf5ae41c607cc7d880dbaa4c9da1a245ab34a","nasal":"4e65838e68bcc8818c7c7cad5e5216af8d5196db3f7daec04c5a62ad69a30f87"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":6,"english":"And in that limitless gloom, the Rākṣasas, transported with wrath, advanced with impetuous speed, devouring monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.771,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d08c2dd26c4e6a40b1f056dbb14aa87345c7ebd2719f251e5e536a9be066e7aa","compact":"c83654b5905192cba743afbcf2ede49b0fb6d1b9490d6db3a284767bff500fc1","nasal":"01e4fe39b3f53a3b119c4273bf8f34e58b10588988c3535c367b85e0e2a7e960"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":7,"english":"And, fired with terrible wrath, they, bounding up, with their sharp tecih tore up steeds caparisoned in gold, and standards resembling venomous serpents. *i.e. the monkeys, as appears from the context.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.653,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a2079bcac99591fd40ff79125f881f2cc218f07bee858bacd79935b4ff0cb444","compact":"f522dd51c97a52713fc541c1cb661179b276040c1c0445ed6f46078ded0b5774","nasal":"e6ff75914a2ba26de78e538297f5e44003fed96ece013be587ddb3eb29983bf0"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":8,"english":"The lusty monkeys in battle agitated the Rāks asa host, and, waxing furious, with their teeth pulled and bit elephants and the riders there of, and cars furnished with flags and standards.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.824,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"56f0e1e6e5052e157e0beaeb61070e47827d4b1c4865e0666fdb943836f92296","compact":"fbc7445857496ff55b59759bca81c5835ca8989a90fd7755d220e0260b51a4fc","nasal":"23e06264a8dc6e7f61259f15b73da9365809e3e75e2cae5635f9ad843723b4e8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":9,"english":"Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa with shafts resembling venomous serpents, slaughtered the foremost among the Rakşasas-both those that were seen and those that were not.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"598d0804dbacd58f479b0ffd9b846b140e66ed868047154272f8ec61db0985fb","compact":"19b809e31b768eeb3813e0ceff7a1215d8efc3f306055122265e41f8f045982b","nasal":"19b809e31b768eeb3813e0ceff7a1215d8efc3f306055122265e41f8f045982b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":10,"english":"The dust of the earth arising from warring combatants, and from the hoofs of horses and the wheels of cars, choked up eye and ear.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.678,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0ed44e3e014c46e99d2127b18ad8e7c906146189c5570783b45da43bc5eaabdd","compact":"980a6cc34153de36c9225bf9fc3ad674ecad0227430869631bd8f4c74b3afe4c","nasal":"980a6cc34153de36c9225bf9fc3ad674ecad0227430869631bd8f4c74b3afe4c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":11,"english":"And as the mighty envounter, capable of making people's hair stand on end, went on, there flowed a fearful river of gore.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.419,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e6fbf8bd371eb541311dd0952dac2c36dcc649731bce31a8d1dae0f10a781178","compact":"c89cc33dff1eb0cbbd8f8872a10c72f885dc5639c84ab4e9db58636d189574f3","nasal":"c89cc33dff1eb0cbbd8f8872a10c72f885dc5639c84ab4e9db58636d189574f3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":12,"english":"The sounds of kettle-drums and Mşdangas and Panavas, mingled with those of conchs and carwheels, were wonderful (to hear).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.71,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7af237e11730c16c2f7ace52e2b4d894cfae1a8291a683c97729a47e3fdd6be8","compact":"3cc2b3803ed8d5e12e93c2584042177f5e84dea813f3bda9be27b204f239a0a7","nasal":"f2e15f3c903d18ddea9768ec756af8c427fa8a59958cbd6f7c0b69036f118bd1"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":13,"english":"The sounds of steeds neighing, and Rāks asas (roaring) and monkeys, rejoicing, were something tremendous.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.677,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d3cc6fe07f280247af6e10ccd1204d5897517403aa8383287c01e56c78fb3f6a","compact":"7dd8d96cf1b76aab5d8d7ef18addf76a738e569c8f18d0d258ae0766dc153ae9","nasal":"7dd8d96cf1b76aab5d8d7ef18addf76a738e569c8f18d0d258ae0766dc153ae9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":14,"english":"And, with able monkeys slain; and darts and javelins and axes; and slaughtered Raksasa wearing forms at pleasure, lying mountain likethe field of battle, seeming to have offerings of arms representing flowers, became difficult to recognise, and inaccessible; and the earth was drenched with streams of blood.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.529,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0ec3e80bb79e36fb343d98ea07313e30b81f079a55ec91fee2ab3566a6084b76","compact":"9eea88e031dc3c22446d4ca794f541d570b036a5e49465d14b84858099dfb481","nasal":"9eea88e031dc3c22446d4ca794f541d570b036a5e49465d14b84858099dfb481"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":15,"english":"That Night, destructive to monkeys and Rākş asas, was dreadful, and difficult of being outsped by all, like to the Fatal Night of beings.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8d291b6f6bebda72c7855ee3698141f334d358954e788d7988f958514192c93c","compact":"15936ae2c81ee7ad82dc996b3e81515eb25f3cdbd63f166dab2d540eb66fdcdf","nasal":"15936ae2c81ee7ad82dc996b3e81515eb25f3cdbd63f166dab2d540eb66fdcdf"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":16,"english":"And in that attacked Rama with a shower of shafts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2a090cab978ba0f28b6f2be63efa45a64b73a13dce3b6cbda2ac41c84e19c2a6","compact":"c75833314d5f92d38ddc91505f2b37eeda7a9a057570961135a1b197f118a340","nasal":"e6a028042a7076d3fd37af0cca875e21c1bc0bcd55c5783ab2be7b6139d6dc69"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":17,"english":"The roars of those beings as they advanced, sending up shouts in anger, resembled the dashing of the Ocean at the time of the universal dissolution.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.591,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6a9ed63e1d1624c642d2f5f5fa1161f1c1bbeefa99b9b62ea5f954da17bf47bb","compact":"752fe3cc71ae57dbcff0ffa6fe047e9f4159b2b0c0201457aaf6e7a4592c76e7","nasal":"752fe3cc71ae57dbcff0ffa6fe047e9f4159b2b0c0201457aaf6e7a4592c76e7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":18,"english":"In the twinkling of an eye, Räma by means of six shafts resembling tongues of flames, struck six of the night-rangers, viz., Yajñaśatru, irrepressible (in fight), and Mahaparsva, and Mahodara, and the huge bodied Vajradanstra, and those two-Suka and Sarana. Then in the twinkling of an eye, that Mahāratha rendered all sides clear (of all gloom) by means of arrows resembling tongues of fire; and those other heroic Raksasas that were in front of Rāma, were destroyed on approaching the place, like insects approaching a fire.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-18","DUTT-6-44-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"77f095407568a31323ec8a0360ed4d4fe53e1b5c0090883c4579b8d7371838c9","compact":"2def225c38844c35cc669ceea5e7c66a3df6337669f129e63cb1c17ec70e7e33","nasal":"f8ea4837ed2ac63d9c41f1ae9deb06e254a980ab2c42ac1ec6bdfd3bc6b2bb23"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":19,"english":"In the twinkling of an eye, Räma by means of six shafts resembling tongues of flames, struck six of the night-rangers, viz., Yajñaśatru, irrepressible (in fight), and Mahaparsva, and Mahodara, and the huge bodied Vajradanstra, and those two-Suka and Sarana.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1893ae6c3942aacca381507f6ee25e1a607c7e4083de3c7485153c221e884f61","compact":"d653bc7aa7007057cdbe456f273c360a18d6dbcf8ce10fd6ecfcddef083780e3","nasal":"d653bc7aa7007057cdbe456f273c360a18d6dbcf8ce10fd6ecfcddef083780e3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":20,"english":"And, pierced in their vitals with Rama's shafts, they, having only their lives left to them, disappeared from the field.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c7d77d2d0877361200209575925d35e200871db1580ebbfe26804d8c11550d03","compact":"9e47bc1be23b8dd1d3a53f9df4648000f8295faa44fbaef9523700fb33819b82","nasal":"9e47bc1be23b8dd1d3a53f9df4648000f8295faa44fbaef9523700fb33819b82"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":21,"english":"Then in the twinkling of an eye, that Mahāratha rendered all sides clear (of all gloom) by means of arrows resembling tongues of fire; and those other heroic Raksasas that were in front of Rāma, were destroyed on approaching the place, like insects approaching a fire.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.593,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-44-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6034021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"54ab07fa784e1336870d73de2f040382fd41d786baee0d0f586bfce60df5dab0","compact":"4a0923a8c32e1c927ac8b6f04fa211ea7c9cc3069a58be4f4474f0842f430cd9","nasal":"1e43a244e6d70be56daec6d959e161fe475af21285242d12afa881bb8b6be7ab"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-34-22","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":34,"verse":22,"english":"Then in the twinkling of an eye, that Mahāratha rendered all sides clear (of all gloom) by means of arrows resembling tongues of fire; and those other heroic Raksasas that were in front of Rāma, were destroyed on approaching the place, like insects approaching a fire.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DU